config: USE stacking applies the remembered effect of each configuration layer

Sub-series: O (stage 4, round 2) - patch 3 of 3; needs 0012 (it calls _regenerate_use_stack() of that patch).
Base: upstream 73646c35d.

_regenerate_use_stack() replays every token of every layer (profile defaults,
make.conf, package.use, ...) for each new combination of inputs; the make.conf
layer alone is about 260 tokens and nine USE_EXPAND resets and is the same for
every package. A layer without a token that prints a warning or looks at IUSE is
a sequence of four kinds of steps (add a flag, discard a flag, discard a prefix,
clear), each of which treats every flag independently. Its effect on any
starting set is therefore (clear, discards, strips, adds), with adds computed by
the unchanged loop itself from the empty set. _regenerate_use_stack_fast()
applies that tuple per layer and hands any other layer, alone and with the
flags so far, to the unchanged loop.

Judge: see 0033 (measured together); alone 86.0 against 87.2 s (three passes,
inside the noise). Lock-step counters of the author: 12,398 stack comparisons,
0 mismatches. See 0032 for origin and for why there is no author report.
Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in stage 4 of the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-21, on
upstream commit 73646c35d with patches 0001-0030 and the C modules applied. Not a
human-written change. Judge: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of one system image, six
resolves in parallel, wall seconds summed; every run gave the same merge list in the same
order and the same number of backtracking attempts as unpatched 73646c35d. Black-box
testers (invented states, reference against candidate): 0 differences.

Ported to upstream bdf046b03 (2026-11-23) by a three-way merge per file (base 73646c35d).

